==Passive effect==
The staff has a unique [[passive effect]] that grants the built in spell [[Life leech]] properties. [[Successful hit]]s with the spell have a 1/5 ''(20%)'' chance of dealing 8 additional damage and healing the user half the amount of [[hitpoints]] dealt to a target. This healing effect has a visible 'upwards spiral' on the enemy when triggered.

The percentage of damage healed can be calculated with the following formula:

<math>\begin{align}
\text{Percentage of damage healed} &= \frac{(\text{Max Hit} / 2) + 8}{10 * (\text{Max Hit} / 2 + 1.6)} * 100 \\
\end{align}</math>

With a max mage setup and a saturated heart, the staff heals the user for approximately 12.5% of damage dealt.

==Uses==
[[File:Sanguinesti staff passive effect.gif|thumb|250px|A player attack triggers the staff's passive effect.]]
Compared to the [[trident of the swamp]], the built-in spell hits two damage higher with a maximum base damage of 35 compared to the trident of the swamp's 33. The trident possesses the ability to [[venom|envenom]], while the staff possesses the healing passive effect.

Thus, the staff is most optimal in situations where venom or poison has no benefit and where healing is required. However, if the player's target is not immune to venom, players could initially use the trident of the swamp against the target until the target has been envenomed, then switch to the Sanguinesti staff. Notable encounters where the staff's healing capability proves very useful include the [[Kraken]], the [[Chambers of Xeric]], [[Dagannoth Rex]], [[Zulrah]], [[Nightmare]], [[The Whisperer]], and the [[Tombs of Amascut]].

==Charging==
To use the staff's magic spell, it must be charged with [[blood rune]]s, holding up to 20,000 charges when fully charged. Each cast requires 2 blood runes, costing {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Blood rune|2}}|c}} per cast. Players can configure the charges while the weapon is in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials. The total cost to fully charge the staff with 40,000 blood runes is {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Blood rune|40000}}|c}}. Assuming non-stop use, with one cast every 2.4 seconds equalling 1,500 casts per hour, the staff costs {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Blood rune|2}}* 1500|c}} per hour to use.

